A||N||4||mutfish||CLUTH CHATTER||||1
Z||000000||mutfish||10-21-1999||10:35 PM||||Have an 88 GT with moderate to severe cluth chatter,mostly in 1st gear, in reverse it's barely noticeable in reverse...any clues?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||10-23-1999||04:26 AM||||There are a few clutch threads on this forum and they go into incredible detail about possible clutch problems. Just search on "clutch" and they'll pop up.<P>PS: bring lots of food and water - some of those threads are quite long!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-25-1999||12:20 AM||||It is most likely a friction disk about to come apart.  Glazing on the flywheel and pressure plate would also cause this.<BR>Mine chattered for a while until I had time to pull the engine/cradle and pull the clutch out.  My flywheel was slightly glazed and the friction disk only had two patches of friction material left about the size of a silver dollar.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Thomas||10-25-1999||04:54 AM||||I thing you nees a new clutch in the next.<BR>In the last years i swap my cluch 3 times.<BR>(next month again):-((<BR>Every time before my clutch go faulty i´ve got the same symptoms.Noise at shifting in the first gear and a little bit later at reverse too.<BR>The clutch plate is oftly not down, but the bearing or the relever or releverplate are down.<BR>But before you change the clutch:<BR>Check for air in the hydraulic line.<BR>Look for loosen nuts at shifting cable.<BR>Look for leaking slave cylinder.<P>I hate the Fiero clutch. My biggest problem at the fiero. :-))||||reg||1
Z||000004||mutfish||10-25-1999||08:45 AM||||Thanks everyone for the input...it's what I expected to hear. I'm in the process of painting it right now, after that I'll replace the clutch setup.||||reg||14
